# Shell scripts must keep LF endings whatever the checkout platform: a CRLF
# shebang fails with "bad interpreter", and openandroiddex-wmd/build.sh is run
# by `npm run apk` on every macOS and Linux build.
#
# (openandroiddex-launcher/.gitattributes says the same for its Gradle wrapper,
# for exactly this reason.)
*.sh text eol=lf

# `npm run tauri dev` writes the app's Cargo.toml back with LF endings every time
# it starts (the Tauri CLI's manifest rewrite). Checked out with CRLF on Windows
# (core.autocrlf), git then lists it as modified with no change in it: LF here too.
open-android-dex-tauri/src-tauri/Cargo.toml text eol=lf
